[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"still image"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Art"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Criticism, interpretation, etc."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2019"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2019"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Lund Humphries,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2019."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"103 pages : illustrations (some colour) ; 29 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Color content","#text":"polychrome"}}],"abstract":"This is the sixth volume in Lund Humphries' series of monographs on British sculptor Anthony Caro and the first publication to focus on his use of stainless steel as a distinct body of work.0Caro employed stainless steel extensively, from intimately scaled Table Sculptures to extremely large works, over many decades, and in his mature works, Caro's exploration and interrogation of this material became increasingly important. 0Karen Wilkin analyses Caro's use of stainless steel in the context of the development of modernist constructed sculpture, pioneered in the UK by Caro and in the US by David Smith, a friend and admired predecessor, from whom Caro inherited most of the stainless steel he first employed, following Smith's untimely death in 1965. 0Karen Wilkin's text represents a much-needed overview of Caro's late career and a vital expansion of our understanding of 20th-century and early 21st-century modernist sculpture.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Karen Wilkin."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (page 102) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Metal sculpture"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Sculpture, British"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Sculpture, Modern"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Stainless steel","In art"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Sculpture en métal"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Sculpture britannique"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Acier inoxydable","Dans l'art"]},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Stainless steel"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Sculpture, Modern"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Sculpture, British"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Metal sculpture"},{"@authority":"gnd","topic":"Stahlplastik"},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Caro, Anthony,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1924-2013"}]},"topic":"Criticism and interpretation"},{"@authority":"fast","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Caro, Anthony,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1924-2013"}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJjMC9p3wMjhBfYhHrQrMP"}},{"@authority":"gnd","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Caro, Anthony",{"@type":"date","#text":"1924-2013"}]}}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"NB497.C35 W55 2019"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"730.92"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"constituent","titleInfo":{"title":"Works. Selections"},"name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Caro, Anthony,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1924-2013"}]}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99153847937103941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781848223486"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"184822348X"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"1111296637"}],"locat